# IMAP monitor patch compatibility record.
# install.sh / update-and-reapply.sh read tested_against_upstream and compare it to the
# upstream tag they are about to build against; on a mismatch they print a WARNING and
# continue (per spec: warn, never block). update-and-reapply.sh updates this file after a
# staging rehearsal against a new upstream tag passes.
patch_version=1.0.0
tested_against_upstream=2.5.6
last_verified_date=2026-10-11
notes=Built, verified, staged and promoted to production against Uptime Kuma 2.4.0 on 2026-10-11, then updated to 2.5.6 the same day via update-and-reapply.sh (build/stage/test/uninstall-rehearsal repeated against a fresh production snapshot, then promoted) - the full update-resistance workflow this patch layer exists for, proven end to end against a real production instance. The patch needed rework for 2.5.6: upstream inserted new monitor types (steam registry entry, pm2, sftp, ntp) adjacent to every one of this patch's insertion points, breaking git apply's context matching without changing the semantics - resolved by re-deriving the same edits against a fresh 2.5.6 clone. STARTTLS mode is still verified by code review and against a local greenmail test server only (no live STARTTLS-capable server available at mailbox.souver.nl).
